  M4 CANDIDATE [D-talk-request gen_fqmp62x turns=10 naturalEnd=true]:
    NPC: "Can we talk?" Vikram sits down near you. "Just... talk. Like people used to."
    NPC: "Help me haul something back? Too much for one."
    YOU: "All right. Let's go."
    NPC: Vikram shows you where they go to think. "Don't tell the others. Everyone needs one place."
    YOU: "I’m listening."
    NPC: "...Hi. Sorry. I'm not good at the talking-to-strangers part."
    YOU: "Neither am I, honestly."
    NPC: Something eases in their shoulders. "Oh. Okay. That's... that's fine, then."
    YOU: "Take your time."
    NPC: A warmth settles over the conversation — they lean in a little.
    YOU: "Take your time."
    NPC: "Strangers are just people you haven't disappointed yet. That's what my mother said. Terrible advice, but it got me through parties."
    YOU: "What do you think it means?"
    YOU: "What do you think is actually going on here?"
    NPC: "Every ability I've seen has a cost. Find the cost, manage the cost, and the thing's just another tool."
    YOU: (listen)
    NPC: "Anyway." A small smile.
    YOU: (listen)
    NPC: "So." They look at the fire for a moment.
    YOU: "I'm here. Go on."
    NPC: "Alright, love. Go do what you need to do."
    YOU: "..."
    NPC: You say nothing. Neither do they, for a while — and it's fine.
    NPC: "Good talk. I feel like I know you a little better now."
    NPC: "Good — the big questions, settled. Feels better said out loud."
    NPC: They're smiling as you go. "Come back anytime."

