  M4 CANDIDATE [D-talk-request gen_g6zxb0p turns=11 naturalEnd=true]:
    NPC: "You talk to it -- the System. Have you ever asked? About the taken -- about Daniel?"
    YOU: "Yes."
    NPC: "I see." They take a moment to think about your answer.
    YOU: "Yeah?"
    NPC: They take it in and give nothing back. Not yet.
    YOU: "Yeah?"
    NPC: "Did you sleep? I kept hearing things out past the treeline."
    YOU: "I heard them too."
    NPC: They go still. "So it's not just me. Good. That's... good to know. Bad, but good."
    YOU: "Yeah?"
    NPC: "I sleep in shifts now — two hours, up, listen, two more. My body learned it before my head agreed. Columbus, Ohio never taught me that. The treeline did."
    YOU: "Tell me about them."
    NPC: "It's my grandfather, Daniel. Went in the Taking. He survived two wars and a famine. Not interesting enough, apparently. The pods get into my sleep some nights.
    NPC: Row on row of them, humming like a held note -- and I wake up reaching for something that isn't there."
    YOU: "I'll ask the System about the pods."
    NPC: "You'd do that? Ask it? ...Thank you. Really. Even asking is more than the silence."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "Still on that taken person. — ask anyone!"
    YOU: "Yeah?"
    NPC: A warmth settles over the conversation — they lean in a little.
    YOU: "Yeah?"
    NPC: "Okay. We'll pick this up later."
    YOU: "..."
    NPC: A comfortable quiet settles. They smile a little, and let it be.
    NPC: "If it answers -- you'll tell me? Whatever it says. I can take it."
    NPC: They're smiling as you go. "Come back anytime."

